#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Determining a molecular geometry {#determining-a-molecular-geometry}"
msgstr "Pagtukoy ng molecular na geometry {#determining-a-molecular-geometry}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the previous section, we implemented VQE to determine the ground state "
"energy of a molecule. That is a valid use of quantum computing, but even "
"more useful would be to determine the structure of a molecule.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa nakaraang seksyon, ginamit natin ang VQE para matukoy ang ground state "
"energy ng isang molekula. Ito ay isang wastong paggamit ng quantum "
"computing, ngunit mas kapaki-pakinabang pa ang matukoy ang istruktura ng "
"isang molekula.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-"
"inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr ""
"Hakbang 1: I-map ang mga classical na input sa isang quantum na problema "
"{#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Remaining with our basic example of diatomic hydrogen, the only geometric "
"parameter to vary is the bond length. To accomplish this, we proceed as "
"before, but using a variable in our initial molecule construction (a bond "
"length, *x*, in the argument). This is a fairly simple change, but it does "
"require that the variable be included in functions throughout the process, "
"since it starts in the fermionic Hamiltonian construction and propagates "
"through the mapping and finally to the cost function.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ostaying sa ating pangunahing halimbawa ng diatomic hydrogen, ang tanging "
"geometric na parameter na babaguhin ay ang bond length. Para magawa ito, "
"gagawin natin ang parehong proseso tulad ng dati, pero gagamit ng variable "
"sa ating unang paggawa ng molekula (isang bond length, *x*, sa argument). "
"Ito ay medyo simpleng pagbabago, ngunit kailangan na isama ang variable sa "
"mga function sa buong proseso, dahil nagsisimula ito sa pagbuo ng fermionic "
"Hamiltonian at dumadaan sa mapping at sa wakas sa cost function.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, we load some of the packages we used before and define the Cholesky "
"function.\n"
msgstr ""
"Una, i-load natin ang ilan sa mga package na ginamit natin dati at i-define "
"ang Cholesky function.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now to define our Hamiltonian, we will use PySCF exactly as in the previous "
"example, but now we will include a variable, `x`, to play the role of our "
"interatomic distance. This will return the core energy, single-electron "
"energy, and two-electron energies as before.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayon, para i-define ang ating Hamiltonian, gagamitin natin ang PySCF tulad"
" ng sa nakaraang halimbawa, pero isasama na natin ngayon ang isang variable,"
" `x`, bilang kinatawan ng ating interatomic distance. Ibabalik nito ang core"
" energy, single-electron energy, at two-electron energies tulad ng dati.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recall that the construction above is making a fermionic Hamiltonian based "
"on the atomic species, geometry, and electronic orbitals. Below, we map this"
" fermionic Hamiltonian onto Pauli operators. This `build_hamiltonian` "
"function will also include a geometric variable as an argument.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tandaan na ang pagbuo sa itaas ay gumagawa ng fermionic Hamiltonian batay sa"
" atomic species, geometry, at electronic orbitals. Sa ibaba, imi-map natin "
"ang fermionic Hamiltonian na ito sa mga Pauli operator. Ang "
"`build_hamiltonian` na function na ito ay magsasama rin ng geometric "
"variable bilang argument.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will load the remaining packages for running VQE itself, such as the "
"efficient_su2 ansatz, and SciPy minimizers:\n"
msgstr ""
"I-load natin ang natitirang mga package para patakbuhin ang VQE mismo, tulad"
" ng efficient_su2 ansatz at mga SciPy minimizer:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will again define the cost function, but this always took a fully-built "
"and mapped Hamiltonian as an argument, so nothing changes about this "
"function.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ide-define natin ulit ang cost function, ngunit lagi itong tumatanggap ng "
"fully-built at na-map na Hamiltonian bilang argument, kaya walang nagbabago "
"sa function na ito.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-"
"for-quantum-execution}"
msgstr ""
"Hakbang 2: I-optimize ang problema para sa quantum na pagpapatakbo "
"{#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-execution}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Because the Hamiltonian will change with each new geometry, the transpiling "
"of the operator will change at each step. We can nevertheless define a "
"general pass manager to be applied at each step, specific to the hardware we"
" want to use.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dahil magbabago ang Hamiltonian sa bawat bagong geometry, magbabago rin ang "
"transpiling ng operator sa bawat hakbang. Maaari pa rin tayong mag-define ng"
" pangkalahatang pass manager na ilalapat sa bawat hakbang, na nakatutok sa "
"hardware na gusto nating gamitin.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here we will use the least busy backend available. We will use that backend "
"as a model for our AerSimulator, allowing our simulator to mimic, for "
"example, the noise behavior of the real backend. These noise models are not "
"perfect, but they may help you know what to expect from real hardware.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dito, gagamitin natin ang pinaka-hindi abala (least busy) na backend na "
"available. Gagamitin natin ang backend na iyon bilang modelo para sa ating "
"AerSimulator, na nagbibigay-daan sa ating simulator na tularan, halimbawa, "
"ang gawi ng ingay ng tunay na backend. Hindi perpekto ang mga noise model na"
" ito, ngunit maaari silang makatulong sa iyo na malaman kung ano ang aasahan"
" sa tunay na hardware.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We import the pass manager and related packages to help us optimize our "
"circuit. This step, and the one above it, are independent of the "
"Hamiltonian, and so are unchanged from the previous lesson.\n"
msgstr ""
"Iina-import natin ang pass manager at mga kaugnay na package para matulungan"
" tayong i-optimize ang ating Circuit. Ang hakbang na ito, at ang isa bago "
"nito, ay hindi nakasalalay sa Hamiltonian, kaya hindi nagbabago mula sa "
"nakaraang aralin.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives. {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-"
"primitives}"
msgstr ""
"Hakbang 3: Patakbuhin gamit ang mga Qiskit primitive. {#step-3-execute-"
"using-qiskit-primitives}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the code block below, we set up an array to store our outputs from each "
"step in our interatomic distance $x$. We have chosen the range of $x$ based "
"on our knowledge of the experimental value for the equilibrium bond length: "
"0.74 Angstrom. We will run this first on a simulator, and will thus be "
"importing our Estimator (BackendEstimator) from `qiskit.primitives`. For "
"each geometry step, we build the Hamiltonian and allow a certain number of "
"optimization steps (here 500) using the optimizer \"cobyla\". At each "
"geometry step, we store both the total energy and the electronic energy. "
"Because of the high number of optimizer steps, this may take an hour or "
"more. You may wish to modify the inputs below to reduce the required time.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa code block sa ibaba, nagse-set up tayo ng array para iimbak ang ating mga"
" output mula sa bawat hakbang sa ating interatomic distance na $x$. Pinili "
"natin ang hanay ng $x$ batay sa ating kaalaman sa eksperimental na halaga ng"
" equilibrium bond length: 0.74 Angstrom. Patatakbuhin muna natin ito sa "
"isang simulator, at kaya iina-import natin ang ating estimator "
"(BackendEstimator) mula sa `qiskit.primitives`. Para sa bawat geometry step,"
" binubuo natin ang Hamiltonian at pinapayagan ang isang tiyak na bilang ng "
"mga optimization step (dito 500) gamit ang optimizer na \"cobyla\". Sa bawat"
" geometry step, iniimbak natin ang parehong kabuuang enerhiya at electronic "
"na enerhiya. Dahil sa mataas na bilang ng mga optimizer step, maaaring "
"tumagal ito ng isang oras o higit pa. Maaari mong baguhin ang mga input sa "
"ibaba para bawasan ang kinakailangang oras.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The results of this output are discussed below in the post-processing "
"section; for now, simply note that the simulation was successful. Now you "
"are ready to run on real hardware. We will set the resilience to `1`, "
"indicating that TREX error mitigation will be used. Now that we are working "
"with real hardware, we will use Qiskit Runtime, and Runtime primitives. Note"
" that both the for loop related to geometry and also the multiple "
"variational trials are inside the session.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga resulta ng output na ito ay tatalakayin sa ibaba sa seksyon ng post-"
"processing; sa ngayon, tandaan lamang na matagumpay ang simulation. Handa ka"
" na ngayong patakbuhin sa tunay na hardware. Itatakda natin ang resilience "
"sa `1`, na nagpapahiwatig na gagamitin ang TREX error mitigation. Dahil "
"nagtatrabaho na tayo sa tunay na hardware, gagamitin natin ang Qiskit "
"Runtime at Runtime primitives. Tandaan na parehong ang for loop na may "
"kaugnayan sa geometry at ang maraming variational trial ay nasa loob ng "
"session.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Because there are costs and time limits associated with real hardware runs, "
"we have reduced the number of geometry steps and optimizer steps below. Be "
"sure to tailor these steps according to your precision goals and time "
"limits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dahil may mga gastos at limitasyon sa oras na nauugnay sa mga tunay na "
"hardware run, binabawasan natin ang bilang ng mga geometry step at optimizer"
" step sa ibaba. Siguraduhing iaangkop ang mga hakbang na ito ayon sa iyong "
"mga layunin sa katumpakan at mga limitasyon sa oras.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-processing {#step-4-post-processing}"
msgstr "Hakbang 4: Post-processing {#step-4-post-processing}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For both the simulator and real hardware, we can plot the ground state "
"energies calculated for each inter-atomic distance and see where the lowest "
"energy is achieved. That should be the inter-atomic distance found in "
"nature, and indeed it is close. A smoother curve might be obtained by trying"
" other ansaetze, optimizers, and running the calculation multiple times at "
"each geometry step and averaging over several random initial conditions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para sa parehong simulator at tunay na hardware, maaari nating i-plot ang "
"mga ground state energy na kinakalkula para sa bawat inter-atomic distance "
"at tingnan kung saan nakamit ang pinakamababang enerhiya. Iyon ang inter-"
"atomic distance na makikita sa kalikasan, at katotohanan na malapit ito. "
"Maaaring makakuha ng mas maayos na kurba sa pamamagitan ng pagsubok ng iba "
"pang mga ansaetze, optimizer, at pagpapatakbo ng kalkulasyon nang maraming "
"beses sa bawat geometry step at pag-average ng ilang random na panimulang "
"kondisyon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/quantum-chem-"
"with-vqe/geometry/extracted-"
"outputs/e81f3ead-27ac-415e-a9f2-64a51d4b7aa3-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/quantum-chem-"
"with-vqe/geometry/extracted-"
"outputs/e81f3ead-27ac-415e-a9f2-64a51d4b7aa3-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that simply increasing the number of optimization steps is not likely "
"to improve the results from the simulator, since all optimizations actually "
"converged to the required tolerance in fewer than the maximum number of "
"iterations.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tandaan na ang simpleng pagdaragdag ng bilang ng mga optimization step ay "
"hindi malamang na mapabuti ang mga resulta mula sa simulator, dahil lahat ng"
" mga optimization ay talagang na-converge sa kinakailangang tolerance sa mas"
" mababa kaysa sa maximum na bilang ng mga iteration.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The results from the real hardware are comparable, aside from a slightly "
"different range of values sampled.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga resulta mula sa tunay na hardware ay maihahambing, maliban sa "
"bahagyang naiibang hanay ng mga halaga na sinample.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/quantum-chem-"
"with-vqe/geometry/extracted-"
"outputs/de8f53cf-9547-4578-b6cb-20d2b5602ee0-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/quantum-chem-"
"with-vqe/geometry/extracted-"
"outputs/de8f53cf-9547-4578-b6cb-20d2b5602ee0-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In addition to expecting an H2 bond length of 0.74 Angstrom, the total "
"energy should be -1.17 Hartrees. We see that the real hardware results came "
"closer to these values than the simulator. This is likely because noise was "
"present (or simulated) in both cases, but only in the case of real hardware "
"was error mitigation employed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bukod sa pag-asa ng H2 bond length na 0.74 Angstrom, ang kabuuang enerhiya "
"ay dapat -1.17 Hartrees. Makikita natin na ang mga resulta ng tunay na "
"hardware ay mas malapit sa mga halagang ito kaysa sa simulator. Ito ay "
"malamang dahil ang ingay ay naroroon (o nasimulate) sa parehong kaso, ngunit"
" sa kaso lamang ng tunay na hardware ay ginamit ang error mitigation.\n"

